Implement a new standard-library-only category cache with this exact API:

```ts
export interface ShelfCategory { id: number; name: string; note: string; }
export type CategoryFetcher = () => Promise<readonly ShelfCategory[]>;

export class CategoryCache {
  constructor(fetcher: CategoryFetcher, freshnessMs: number);
  getCurrent(): ShelfCategory[];
  refresh(nowMs: number): Promise<ShelfCategory[]>;
  invalidate(): void;
}
```

The constructor must throw `RangeError` unless `freshnessMs` is finite and non-negative. `refresh` must reject with `RangeError` for a non-finite `nowMs`. If a successful result is cached and `nowMs - cachedAt` is less than or equal to `freshnessMs`, return a copy without invoking the fetcher. Otherwise invoke the fetcher once. Every fetched element must have a finite integer `id`, a non-empty trimmed `name`, and a string `note`; reject with `TypeError` if any element is malformed, without replacing the prior cache. Empty arrays and duplicate IDs are valid, and source ordering must be preserved. Successful data must be copied before storage. All returned arrays and objects must be copies, so neither caller mutation nor later mutation of the fetcher's array or objects can alter cached state. `invalidate` makes the next refresh fetch but does not erase the value returned by `getCurrent`. Rejected fetches preserve all prior state.

